// The one instantiation queue (plan 11 B11.2): generic fns, generic struct methods, `dyn` vtables,
// `#[impl]` bound checks and `derive` methods are each "instance requested at span S", drained to a fixed
// point after bodies are typed. Demand-driven: only what is reached gets typed and lowered.
//
// Part of module j3c.sema.
// Port of: (new; replaces Rust's `bound_queue`, `lazy_methods` + `wake` in `check/lower/lazy.rs`,
// `take_new_vtables`, and `fn_insts` bookkeeping)
// J3: Instance keys are `(item, []Ty)` interned once; the requesting span is kept for errors, so a bound
// failure in an instance points at the use that asked for it, as Rust's text does.
module j3c.sema;
